Comments:
Evaluated by Caleb Marshall, 2024
1) Sub-threshold resonance parameters derived from (a, g) strengths of Schmalbrock 1983 and total widths/total width upper limits,
   G_g / G from Vermeer 1988, proton widths of Marshall 2023, and total widths of Goldberg 1954 with a factor of 2 uncertainty
   for values in parenthesis.  Upper limit on 38.3 keV is from Hale 2004.
2) Energies are weighted average of ENSDF values (Basunia 2022) and Marshall 2023.
3) 136 keV resonance strength is a weighted average of Boeltzig 2019 and Cerseratto 2013 (interpreted as a positive detection).
4) All higher resonance come from Gorres 1989, Boeltzig 2019, and Switkowski 1975. Switkowski normalized to Paine & Sargood 1979.
   Normalization was avoided in the other cases since the 512 keV resonance was not measured, the standard strength has a large uncertainty,
   and the original studies give reasonable uncertainty estimates. 
5) Direct capture is a unweighted average of Garrett 1978, Fuchs 1968, Hale 2004, and Marshall 2023. Uncertainties increased to 50%
   based on observations of Boeltzig 2022 and discrepancy between Hale/Marshall and Garrett. Garrett and Fuchs were ignored when
   only a single C2S value was reported for an energy region known to have multiple, strong states.